course: dictionary
lesson: 5925
title: Marseille: a city by the sea
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Marseille is a big city on the coast of southern France, beside the Mediterranean Sea. It is a port, a place where ships load and unload, so the city is full of boats. «Marseilles, in the south of France, was founded by Greek sailors about 2,600 years ago, which makes it one of the oldest cities in France.» The word oldest tells you it is very old.
explain: You may see two spellings: Marseille, the French spelling, and Marseilles, an older English spelling. Both name the same city. The name comes from French, so use the French spelling when you write it in French lessons.
explain: «La Marseillaise» is the French national anthem, which means it is the country's official song. It is named after soldiers from Marseille who sang it in 1792. In French lessons, you say the name «mar-SAY».
fact: Marseille is a large port city on the Mediterranean coast in southern France.
fact: Marseille is the second-largest city in France.
fact: Greek sailors founded Marseille about 600 BC, so it is one of the oldest cities in France.
fact: «Marseilles» is an older English spelling of the French name Marseille.
fact: «La Marseillaise» is named after soldiers from Marseille who sang it in 1792.
exercise: Which country is Marseille in? | *France | Italy | Germany | Spain
exercise: Marseille is a port. What does port mean here? | A dark forest | *A place where ships load and unload | A strong wind from the north | A kind of hot drink
exercise: «Marseilles ... was founded by Greek sailors about 2,600 years ago.» Find and copy one word that means started or set up. | *founded | sailors | Greek | oldest
test: Which sea is Marseille beside? | North Sea | *Mediterranean | Red Sea | Black Sea
test: Why is Marseille called one of the oldest cities in France? | *Because it was founded about 2,600 years ago | Because it has the most tall buildings | Because it is the capital of France | Because it is high in the mountains
exam: «La Marseillaise» is named after whom? | A ship's captain | *Soldiers from Marseille who sang it in 1792 | A famous French king | Greek sailors who founded the city
